# Maintainer public keys (tag + attestation verification)

Tag-signing and identity keys for [@kudosscience](https://github.com/kudosscience)
(Henry Ward, maintainer / RSO). Import this file, then `git verify-tag`
passes without trusting any server we run.

- GPG fingerprint: `D23D 4D17 9B4C 1D45 25BB A1EF AA5A EB73 13B2 A916`
  (key id `AA5AEB7313B2A916`, created 2026-09-08, expires 2028-09-07, `[SC]`).
  GitHub also lists this key on the maintainer's profile as verified.
- SSH signing key (`gpg.format=ssh`): see
  `.github/trusted-keys/maintainer-ssh.pub` (same key below, plus
  `.github/trusted-keys/allowed_signers` for `git verify-tag`).

Verify a safety tag with GPG:

```sh
gpg --import docs/safety/MAINTAINER_PUBKEYS.asc
git verify-tag safety/v0.2.0
```

Verify a safety tag with SSH signatures (when `gpg.format=ssh` was used):

```sh
git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile .github/trusted-keys/allowed_signers
git verify-tag safety/v0.2.0
```

Key rotation: append the new key here (never delete the old one), record
the rotation in `SAFETY.md` Appendix D (Changelog) and the per-release
Risk Report, and re-cut the latest `safety/v*` tag so the chain stays
verifiable. Full end-to-end procedure: `docs/safety/verify-runbook.md`.

Rotation log: on 2026-09-08 the pre-use GPG key `7785 5329 CFC8 2BE2
0807 96E1 B32D 6EFC 6320 085E` was replaced by the key below *before it
ever signed anything* — no signature in the repo references it, so the
append-only rule does not apply. Future rotations of keys that have
signed tags must append, never replace.

